The operations request can't be done within this node's authority. Its `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` and calling `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich` would need filesystem and HTTP capabilities (`http-client`) that the node doesn't hold. The world imports neither, so I left both out. If operations wants them, the graph needs to grant those capabilities to the node first.

I record the considered ids as seen only when the digest was published. An unpublished digest leaves those items eligible to be picked up again on the next run.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;
        if published.published {
            for id in published.considered.iter() {
                state_rw::put(id, &published.date);
                recorded = recorded.saturating_add(1);
            }
        }
        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

